    "model": "Draw a vertical section of the heart viewed from the front (heart's left side on the right of the page), showing: the septum dividing it into left and right sides; two upper chambers (atria) and two lower chambers (ventricles), with the left ventricle wall thicker than the right; and at least one valve (e.g. the bicuspid valve between the left atrium and left ventricle, and/or the tricuspid valve on the right). Labels (1 mark each): Aorta = the large artery leaving the top of the left ventricle and arching over the heart; Bicuspid valve = the two-flapped valve between the left atrium and left ventricle; Left ventricle = the thick-walled lower chamber on the left side (right of the page).",
