    "model": "I put on gloves, lab coat and safety glasses and washed the heart under cold water. I placed it on a dissecting board/tray and identified the front, which has a coronary artery running diagonally across it; the left ventricle felt firmer than the right. I cut with scissors from the right atrium down the wall of the right ventricle, and opened the left side the same way, to expose the internal structures (e.g. the tricuspid and bicuspid valves). I labelled what I saw, drew it, and then disposed of the heart as directed and disinfected the board and instruments, keeping cutting away from my fingers throughout.",
