    "label": "(c)(iv)",
    "marks": 12,
    "model": "NADH delivers high-energy electrons (and protons) to the start of the chain. The electrons are passed from carrier to carrier along the chain in the inner mitochondrial membrane. At each transfer they lose energy, which is used to make ATP from ADP and Pi. At the end of the chain the low-energy electrons combine with oxygen and H+ to form water (oxygen is the final electron acceptor).",
    "model_source": "notes",
    "answerStatus": "written",
    "type": [
     "long-answer"
    ],
    "diagramRelation": "none",
