    "marks": 3,
    "model": "Slurry and fertiliser washed into rivers and lakes add extra nitrate and phosphate (eutrophication). Algae grow rapidly into a bloom that blocks light, so plants below die. When the algae die, decomposers use up the dissolved oxygen and fish and invertebrates die.",
