    "model": "A quadrat (a square frame of known area) is used. It is placed at a random point in the habitat, e.g. using random-number coordinates on two tape measures laid at right angles. In each quadrat, whether the plant (dandelion, grass) is present or absent is recorded. This is repeated for several quadrats (here 5). The percentage frequency is then calculated: (number of quadrats containing the species / total number of quadrats) x 100.",
